  "additional_concerns": [
    "Scope changes affect the typed answers. node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns OUT_OF_SCOPE when no component is offered; node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and both offer-level candidates do so when the promotional link is false. The questions instead permit a known negative answer that the component or offer is not caught. Preserve this distinction explicitly.",
    "node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5 establishes compliance only within its promotional scope and only with the selected gift control. Its TRUE result does not establish compliance with section 103 or advertising requirements.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional link with an existential non-discount gift classification. They need evidence that the identified gift component shares the relevant promotional link; otherwise separate components could jointly satisfy conditions that no individual component satisfies.",
    "The circular supports the SFC-authorised-fund context, but paragraph 3.11 is quoted in broader investment-product terms. The narrower fund predicates must remain contextual scope choices, not statements of the full Code's coverage.",
    "The supplied packet does not contain the external Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 or the answer to question 1 of the SFC FAQ dated 30 September 2010, referenced in footnote 3. Obtain these authorities for any classification or scope interpretation extending beyond the circular's express summary; no dependency IDs are supplied.",
    "The statutory text of SFO section 103 and the terms of any particular exemption or authorisation are absent. They are needed to determine an actual statutory exception, although not to support the narrow claim that the circular describes alternative exceptions.",
    "No supplied source interval establishes the candidates' temporal applicability. Runtime handling of unavailable facts preserves uncertainty but does not itself establish the legally applicable version."
  ],
